I read the debug file and re-reviewed the live PR #1 at its new head 290f205851d390ddab0b1303cfb74ece651bdd7e. The five requested fixes were applied, all quality gates passed, and the PR remains open/mergeable.

I found two small Core-parity issues remaining, so I would make one final tiny correction before merging.

First, matchP2PK() currently accepts any 33- or 65-byte blob followed by OP_CHECKSIG; it doesn't validate the public-key prefix. Core's MatchPayToPubkey() explicitly calls CPubKey::ValidSize(), and Core's ValidSize() checks that 33-byte keys start with 02/03 and 65-byte keys with 04/06/07. Conveniently, Claude already wrote isPubKeyPush() with exactly this behavior for multisig—matchP2PK() should reuse it.

Second, nextToken() says it mirrors CScript::GetOp for OP_PUSHDATA1/2/4, but it actually implements only PUSHDATA1 and PUSHDATA2; PUSHDATA4 falls into the generic opcode case. This is obscure and probably never appears in QOGE history, but Core's MatchMultisig() consumes pubkeys through GetOp, so a nonminimal PUSHDATA4 pubkey can still structurally reach Core's multisig classifier. Since we're deliberately building a historical explorer rather than only a standard-transaction generator, I'd match Core here too.

